-- Torsor/Cech/meet-pushforward audit, parallel Serre classification round.
-- Twenty-six owned modules; 1237 declarations. The specified H1 quotient
-- has its native module/abelian-group structure. The actual coordinate
-- torsor recovers its cocycle; coboundaries induce equivariant natural
-- isomorphisms with inverse translation by negative coefficients.
-- Equality of canonical H1 classes is equivalent to mere isomorphism
-- for cover-trivial torsors; classes are extracted from mere local sections.
-- Every class is represented using big truncation (no resizing or a small
-- universe of torsors). Zero class is equivalent to a mere global section.
-- Structural torsor records expose displayed carriers; proof constructions
-- remain opaque. Source/target inclusion witnesses are compared explicitly
-- by restriction proof independence, not by opening lattice proof terms.
-- Audited openings are coordinate/group constructions, finite sheaf diagrams,
-- type/subtype and structural carriers, and class maps at characterising
-- equations; no construction proof of extensionality or quotients reopens.
